TCP/IP model
A four-layer networking framework that guides how data moves across the internet, built around the Application, Transport, Internet, and Network Access layers.

The Four Layers of TCP/IP

Application Layer:Interacts directly with user software.Handles high-level protocols like HTTP, FTP, and DNS.

Transport Layer:Manages clean end-to-end data delivery between devices.Uses TCP for reliable delivery or UDP for fast delivery.

Internet Layer:Handles logical IP addressing.Routes packets across different networks to their final target

Network Access Layer:Controls the physical transmission of data.Deals with hardware, cables, and network cards
